      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The finite-slope parahoric p-adic L-function construction develops Shalika local coefficients and their exterior-square factorization, explicit Friedberg-Jacquet test vectors and local zeta integrals, then combines them with overconvergent cohomology and eigenvariety control for the exact interpolation formula. Original parahoric-spherical, regular-refinement and noncritical hypotheses remain explicit. Companion family statements and local polynomial identities are support, not additional counts.",
